  "title": "Félix Lebrun and Chen Yi through at WTT Champions Montpellier as Matsushima survives Qiu",
  "standfirst": "The home favourite and China's Chen Yi won their openers on the first evening, while the top seed, Sora Matsushima, needed an 11-2 decider to get past Germany's Dang Qiu.",
  "body": [
    "Félix Lebrun began his WTT Champions Montpellier campaign with an 11-8, 11-3, 11-3 win over Denmark's Anders Lind in the last 32 on Tuesday evening. Lind made the first game awkward, but once Lebrun had taken it he won 14 of the next 17 points.",
    "Lebrun, who won his first WTT Champions title in Montpellier in 2024, said afterwards that a 3-0 win would give him confidence and that he had incredible memories of the venue. He plays Oh Junsung or Zhou Qihao in the last 16.",
    "Chen Yi lost the first game 12-10 to Taiwan's Peng Yu-han after leading 9-8, then won the next three 11-4, 11-3, 11-5. She meets Wang Manyu or Hana Goda next.",
    "Matsushima led Qiu by two games, then lost the third 11-3 and the fourth 12-10. The world No 1 controlled the decider from the start, took it 11-2, and plays Darko Jorgic or Vladimir Sidorenko in the last 16.",
    "There was a second German defeat in the women's draw, where Romania's Elizabeta Samara beat Han Ying 11-8, 11-4, 8-11, 11-7. Han said her form had felt fine but that something had been missing on the day. Samara joins her compatriot Bernadette Szőcs in the last 16.",
    "The defending champion, Truls Moregard, beat France's Thibault Poret 11-8, 11-6, 11-8 but reached for his shoulder during the third game and paused briefly before serving. He finished the match without further trouble, and it is not clear how serious the problem is. He meets Shunsuke Togami or Tomislav Pucar next.",
    "In the afternoon session Lin Yun-Ju came from 2-1 down to beat Portugal's João Geraldo 8-11, 11-4, 5-11, 11-4, 11-6, winning the fourth game with a run of six points after a timeout."
  ],
